<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64956" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαντικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prophetic, oracular</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1098
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. μυχοί, θρόνοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				180
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				616
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					350.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. φῆμαι</span>
			<i>oracular</i> sayings, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				723
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μ. γένος,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάντεις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1055
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μ. σπέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					520
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐπίπνοια</span>
			<i>prophetic</i> inspiration, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				265b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι μ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				275b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ζῷα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					2.48
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη μ.</span> faculty <i>of divination,
				prophecy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				709
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1274a28
			</span></i>, etc.; more freq. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ
			μαντική</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.68
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ . . μ. ἡ τοῦ
			δαιμονίου</span>, of Socrates, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				40a
			</span></i>: in Poets without Art., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				484
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				311
			</span></i>; also in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαντικὴν Ἀπόλλων ἀνηῦρεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Smp.</u>
					197a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἔνθεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					244b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.103
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>like a prophet, oracular</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. γὰρ εἶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1.115a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phd.</u>
				85b
			</span></i>; 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hes.</u>
				7
			</span></i>. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					1026
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				198a
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
